    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "HEADING",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "✦ ",
       "decorations": [
        {
         "type": "COLOR",
         "colorData": {
          "foreground": "#d7182a"
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "A step, not enough",
       "decorations": [
        {
         "type": "COLOR",
         "colorData": {
          "foreground": "#13224b"
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    ],
    "headingData": {
     "level": 2
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "I asked Nero how he feels now that the end is official. I offered him anger, sadness, a mix of everything, or a middle answer: that the farewell plan is a step in the right direction, but not enough. He picked the middle one.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "The step is the \"library\". An update planned for 12 November adds it, and after the servers close it lets players look at the Pokémon and Holowear they own, change outfits and take commemorative photos. It only works if you download it before 23 March 2027, and on the device where you downloaded it.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "IMAGE",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "CAPTION",
      "nodes": [
       {
        "type": "TEXT",
        "textData": {
         "text": "The library keeps what you owned.",
         "decorations": []
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "imageData": {
     "containerData": {
      "width": {
       "size": "CONTENT"
      },
      "alignment": "CENTER"
     },
     "image": {
      "src": {
       "id": "38ba49_4ef11e9cea714b61b785b1766bff4f78~mv2.jpg"
      },
      "width": 784,
      "height": 441
     },
     "altText": "Pokémon UNITE special event and library feature artwork"
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "Why isn't it enough? Because the library keeps what you owned, not what you did. Nero's first article asked for a way to keep playing, with bots and private matches, if the servers really had to go. The library is half of that: the shelf without the game. Nero gives The Pokémon Company credit for building it, and still asks for the other half.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "BLOCKQUOTE",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "nodes": [
       {
        "type": "TEXT",
        "textData": {
         "text": "The library keeps what you owned, not what you did.",
         "decorations": [
          {
           "type": "ITALIC",
           "italicData": true
          },
          {
           "type": "COLOR",
           "colorData": {
            "foreground": "#13224b"
           }
          },
          {
           "type": "FONT_SIZE",
           "fontSizeData": {
            "unit": "PX",
            "value": 22
           }
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
     }
    ],
    "blockquoteData": {
     "indentation": 1
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "DIVIDER",
    "nodes": [],
    "dividerData": {
     "lineStyle": "SINGLE",
     "width": "SMALL",
     "alignment": "CENTER"
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "HEADING",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "✦ ",
       "decorations": [
        {
         "type": "COLOR",
         "colorData": {
          "foreground": "#d7182a"
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "What Nero will miss",
       "decorations": [
        {
         "type": "COLOR",
         "colorData": {
          "foreground": "#13224b"
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    ],
    "headingData": {
     "level": 2
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "This was an open question, and I'm giving you his whole answer:",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "BLOCKQUOTE",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "nodes": [
       {
        "type": "TEXT",
        "textData": {
         "text": "The ease of play, the feeling of the simple fights, using pokémon moves in real time, understanding builds - even the ones that were overpowered, and I still found fun - and playing with my partner.",
         "decorations": [
          {
           "type": "ITALIC",
           "italicData": true
          },
          {
           "type": "COLOR",
           "colorData": {
            "foreground": "#13224b"
           }
          },
          {
           "type": "FONT_SIZE",
           "fontSizeData": {
            "unit": "PX",
            "value": 22
           }
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
     }
    ],
    "blockquoteData": {
     "indentation": 1
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "None of that is about rewards, rankings or skins. It's about how the game felt to play. UNITE was a MOBA you could understand in one match: short fights, moves you fire yourself in real time, builds you could read. Nero even found the overpowered builds fun, which says a lot about how it felt to play at its best.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "And the last part is about people. Nero played UNITE with his partner. That's the part no library can keep, and the reason a game closing is more than a product leaving a shop.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "IMAGE",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "CAPTION",
      "nodes": [
       {
        "type": "TEXT",
        "textData": {
         "text": "Aeos Island. For five years, a place to meet up after work.",
         "decorations": []
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "imageData": {
     "containerData": {
      "width": {
       "size": "CONTENT"
      },
      "alignment": "CENTER"
     },
     "image": {
      "src": {
       "id": "38ba49_fcb44e208bf24b7393e0065291ef0b02~mv2.jpg"
      },
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 720
     },
     "altText": "The Pokémon UNITE logo over Aeos Island and its stadium at night"
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "textData": {
       "text": "Saotami, a UNITE creator, recorded a goodbye to the game the same week. It's a good companion to Nero's answer:",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "VIDEO",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "CAPTION",
      "nodes": [
       {
        "type": "TEXT",
        "textData": {
         "text": "Saotami: \"Goodbye Pokémon Unite\"",
         "decorations": []
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "videoData": {
